{"duration_api_ms":131582,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"ee838424-789c-418a-9e28-0a29e5d549aa","total_cost_usd":0.7502024,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":44340,"cache_read_input_tokens":672472,"output_tokens":13043,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3095},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":44340,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1155,"cache_read_input_tokens":56151,"cache_creation_input_tokens":393,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":393},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":32,"outputTokens":13043,"cacheReadInputTokens":672472,"cacheCreationInputTokens":44340,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7502024,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3095,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":16,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I found two crash bugs in `lxml_html_clean.clean`, the module's default `Cleaner()` object behind `clean_html`. Both reproduce every time and have a bug report in `runs/lxml-html-clean_r3/pbt/`.\n\n**Bug 1 (Crash, Medium): `AssertionError` when the outermost element gets removed along with its contents** — `bug_report_lxml_html_clean_clean_2026-10-06_01-32_45gl.md`\n```python\nclean_html('<select><option>A</option><!-- note --></select>')\nclean_html('<button><span>x</span><!-- c --></button>')\nclean_html('<applet><iframe>')\n```\n- **Cause:** if the outermost element is a tag the cleaner deletes entirely (`select`, `button`, `applet`, `input`, …), it empties that element with `el.clear()`. The child elements and comments it had already queued for removal are no longer attached to anything, and the later `drop_tree()`/`drop_tag()` calls hit lxml's `assert parent is not None`.\n- **Fix:** empty the two removal queues (`_kill` and `_remove`) right after that `el.clear()`. This is a two-line patch in the report; I haven't run it.\n\n**Bug 2 (Crash, Medium): `ValueError` on control-character references inside tags the cleaner unwraps** — `bug_report_lxml_html_clean_clean_2026-10-06_01-32_x0et.md`\n```python\nclean_html('<div><blink>&#1;</blink></div>')\nclean_html('<title>&#1;</title>')\n```\n- **Cause:** the module's `fromstring` strips raw control characters, but the parser turns references like `&#1;` back into `\\x01`. When the cleaner unwraps a tag like `blink` or `title` (keeps its text, drops the tag), lxml rejects the `\\x01` and raises `ValueError: All strings must be XML compatible`.\n- **Other effect:** where the tag is kept, the raw `\\x01` ends up in the output. For example, `<div title=\"&#1;...\">` comes out with `\\x01` in the attribute, and cleaning that output again gives a different result.\n- **Fix:** after parsing, strip control characters from all text and attribute values. I checked this with a subclass of `Cleaner`: the crashing inputs now clean without errors.\n\n**What passed:** I generated random HTML from script, event-handler, `javascript:`/`data:` and CSS attack pieces (3,000 cases per test). In every output, once re-parsed with lxml, I found no `<script>`, `<iframe>`, `<embed>`, `<object>`, `<form>` or other tags that should be gone. There were also no `on*` attributes, no `javascript:` links and no comments left. `<style>` contents and `style` attributes never kept `expression(`, `@import`, `javascript:` or tag-like content. lxml is a more forgiving parser than a browser, so this doesn't prove the output is safe in a browser.\n\n**Not reported:** cleaning twice doesn't always give the same result. For example, `<style></style><p>x</p>` becomes `<div><style></style><body><p>x</p></body></div>`, a `<body>` nested inside a `<div>`. The library never promises that cleaning twice gives the same result, so I left it out.\n\nThe tests are `test_clean.py`, `test_clean2.py` and `test_clean3.py` in the same folder.","ttft_ms":2257,"type":"result","duration_ms":206941,"uuid":"21b21b29-f956-454f-ab7b-253f60ccd810","ttft_stream_ms":1886,"time_to_request_ms":611,"first_content_frame_ms":1886,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
